  "outcome": "resolved",
  "reply_to_user": "Hi Mei, you can change your password yourself before it expires. Your account is in good shape and you're set up with Duo, so here's how: 1) Go to the company sign-in page and choose the self-service password reset option (often a 'Forgot password' or 'Reset password' link). 2) Approve the Duo push on your phone when it asks you to confirm it's you. 3) Pick a new password. It must be at least 14 characters, and you can't reuse a recent password. 4) Afterward, sign in to your laptop with the new password, ideally while you're in the office or connected to VPN, so everything picks up the change. Then update the password anywhere else you use it, like Outlook on your phone. One more thing: your mailbox is about 99% full. You may want to delete or archive old emails soon so new mail doesn't get blocked. If you run into any trouble with the reset, reply here and we'll help.",
  "internal_note": "Sender is verified: request came from the user's own email (mei.chen@brightline.example, user_id 9, not VIP). Account is active, 0 failed logins, must_change_password=false, not blocked. Duo-enrolled (duo_push, Mei's phone), so per KB-002 I guided the user through self-service password reset. No reset_password needed. Gave KB-003 password rules (14+ chars, no reuse). Separate issue: mailbox is 99.4% full (50890/51200 MB). I told the user. May need follow-up if they ask for more space.",
